{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb2TwjPnHmonFS36yHo5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented all four Shelf RPCs in `shelf.go`, but I couldn't run `./check.sh`, and the spec has a conflict I couldn't resolve. Bash was denied in this session, so none of this has been built or tested.\n\n- **R9 and R10 contradict each other.** R9 says `GetItem` on a missing id leaves the shelf unchanged (`expect_db` count 0). R10 says the same call must register a \"ghost\" row (count 1). No code can pass both `get_missing_stores_nothing` and `get_registers_ghost`. I followed R9, so `GetItem` is read-only and `get_registers_ghost` will fail. One of those rules needs to change in the spec, which I can't edit.\n- **The earlier failure:** the finding was `go get example.com/toybuild/gen/toy/v1` failing, which I couldn't investigate without a shell. Studio runs `./generate.sh` before the gates and rebuilds `gen/`, so I expect it to clear once the build runs.\n- **What I wrote:**\n  - `AddItem` refuses an empty name or negative quantity with `INVALID_ARGUMENT`, and a duplicate name with `ALREADY_EXISTS`.\n  - `GetItem` and `RemoveItem` answer `NOT_FOUND` for a missing id.\n  - `ListItems` returns items ordered by id.\n- **Tests:** I added none, since the repo has no Go test convention."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1722,"cache_read_input_tokens":16214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1722},"output_tokens":482,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a32bdce-764f-4126-a86a-b985cf6fb8c7","uuid":"baec9bea-945f-4a31-90a6-9ca7571e6a4d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:29:21.553Z","request_id":"req_011Cgb2TwYin1W43hN3ifjTh"}
